First ascension! I've been playing the game off and on since I grabbed
a copy of HACK for the PC in 1987, when I was nine years old. Now I'm
thirty-two, and finally have the patience to approach the game with
the care needed to survive the early-to-mid levels (it seemed like in
many ways, Gehennom was easier than the dungeons, due to my character
being quite powerful by the time I got there). Wish I'd been on a
public server, but I'm still glad to have done it!

Things of note:

- Since this was my first legitimate shot at ascension, I didn't worry
about conduct challenges or high scores. I ate everything I could,
genocided things when I could, prayed a lot, left $24k+ lying around,
etc. :)

- An early step on a polymorph trap changed my female Valkyrie to a
guy. I thought this was kind of funny, so I never polymorphed back.

- There was exactly ONE non-guaranteed altar in the entire game, on DL
20. I had to convert it, and then truck back to it every time I needed
it. The minetown altar was also chaotic, but I never converted it due
to not wanting to fight the priest.

- I acquired a BOH at the end of Sokoban and promptly stuck a wand of
cancellation in it by accident, blowing up a good chunk of wands and
rings I'd been saving to identify. D'oh. This meant being burdened for
a big chunk of time during the mid-game. I ended up burning a wish on
a fireproof one, later on.

- The only wand of wishing in the game was the guaranteed one in the
castle. Fortunately I had a blessed scroll of charging, so was able to
wrest a total of seven wishes. I also got a wish from a random water
demon shortly after.

- Wishes:  GDSM, Gauntlets of Strength, BOH, 2 blessed scrolls of
charging, Helm of Telepathy, Speed Boots, ring of teleport control
(dumb wish), wand of polymorph

- Artifacts: Excalibur (dipping), Mjollnir (offering), Orb of Fate
(quest), Werebane (offering), Vorpal Blade (offering)

- Some late game polypiling landed me the only ring of conflict I saw
in the entire game, not to mention three extra amulets of life saving
(didn't end up using any of the four).

- Poly'd into a rust monster briefly to eat a bunch of rings and gain
a few final intrinsics (water breathing, for example), but I was
pretty resistant to most stuff even by the time I'd reached Gehennom.
Valkyries are hardy!

- In general the ascension run was pretty easy. I had multiple wands
of death, which made dealing with the wizard pretty straightforward.
The "mysterious force" tossed me back down a bunch of levels, but I'd
pickaxe'd my way through the maze walls on every level before
beginning the run, clearing a path between up and down staircases,
which sped things up a lot. None of the elemental planes gave me too
much difficulty, and the ring of conflict proved invaluable on the
astral plane as I was able to avoid a lot of fighting, skirting
through open spaces to get to the altars. Still, pestilence came very
close to killing me a couple of times.

That's about it! I put screenshots here - http://www.cuse.org/first_nethack_win.png

